&gt;&gt; First, I wanted to say I love my Ford
Edge.

00:24:16.880 --> 00:24:18.507
It's the best car I've ever owned.

00:24:18.507 --> 00:24:20.082
[SOUND].

00:24:20.082 --> 00:24:24.878
I, and second I, I worked a, a little with
GM during their restructuring.

00:24:24.878 --> 00:24:27.685
And even more than kinda their balance
sheet, what

00:24:27.685 --> 00:24:31.470
I though was the main problem, was the
institutional culture.

00:24:31.470 --> 00:24:33.950
At the company, which was, you know,

00:24:33.950 --> 00:24:37.419
management versus, labor instead of
working together.

00:24:37.419 --> 00:24:41.510
You kind of, see sense of entitlement from
everyone there.

00:24:41.510 --> 00:24:42.679
And from what I understand, when you

00:24:42.679 --> 00:24:45.328
got to, Ford, things weren't all that
different.

00:24:45.328 --> 00:24:49.286
Can you, talk about, maybe tell, some
stories as to what culture's.

00:24:49.286 --> 00:24:49.820
&gt;&gt; Oh, yeah.

00:24:49.820 --> 00:24:53.784
&gt;&gt; Like then, and what you did to, change
the culture.

00:24:53.784 --> 00:24:57.340
and, you know, kind of how you initiate
cultural change from the top down.

00:24:57.340 --> 00:25:01.389
&gt;&gt; Absolutely wow.

00:25:02.780 --> 00:25:06.410
I was thinking that, one of the things
Bill Ford,

00:25:06.410 --> 00:25:08.640
that bill ford was asked one time about
the culture.

00:25:08.640 --> 00:25:11.645
And, I think he used the Kremlin comes to
mind.

00:25:11.645 --> 00:25:12.472
[LAUGH].

00:25:12.472 --> 00:25:16.300
&gt;&gt; From a, you know, past history.

00:25:16.300 --> 00:25:21.540
And, and you imagine what it was like at
Ford, when everybody was regionalized.

00:25:21.540 --> 00:25:23.830
There were no skill teams like engineer
manufacturer, that went

00:25:23.830 --> 00:25:27.260
across the company so there was no way to,
work together.

00:25:27.260 --> 00:25:29.910
And, and everybody was scared.

00:25:31.830 --> 00:25:34.690
It's not going very well, we're losing
money.

00:25:34.690 --> 00:25:37.240
There's not that compelling vision where
we're going,

00:25:37.240 --> 00:25:39.380
There's not actions in place for this,
there.

00:25:39.380 --> 00:25:42.770
So, and, and, And problems with the
vehicles.

00:25:42.770 --> 00:25:44.620
And, so, it was pretty.

00:25:44.620 --> 00:25:49.670
It was a pretty tough environment,
Although, I'd say that, Ford has always

00:25:49.670 --> 00:25:53.140
attracted, the best and the brightest,
over the years, from around the world.

00:25:53.140 --> 00:25:55.190
I mean, none of the Wizkid stories and.

00:25:55.190 --> 00:25:57.450
It's just, it's just this fabulous company
with

00:25:57.450 --> 00:26:01.260
107 year history of, of innovation
throughout the years.

00:26:01.260 --> 00:26:05.040
And so talented people, motivated people.

00:26:05.040 --> 00:26:06.870
But, we didn't have a plan, we didn't have
a vision,

00:26:06.870 --> 00:26:10.620
we didn't have a comprehensive strategy
and, we weren't implementing it.

00:26:10.620 --> 00:26:11.910
So it was pretty, scary.

00:26:11.910 --> 00:26:13.750
And everybody's kind of looking out for
themselves

00:26:13.750 --> 00:26:14.770
and a lot of people were leaving and.

00:26:15.770 --> 00:26:16.270
So

00:26:18.500 --> 00:26:23.440
the only thing that I, I know to do is,
just like my days at Bollingworth.

00:26:23.440 --> 00:26:25.340
We got to pull everybody together.

00:26:25.340 --> 00:26:27.340
We need a compelling vision, about where
we're going, so we

00:26:27.340 --> 00:26:31.130
all understand where we're going, so then
all the actions are explainable.

00:26:31.130 --> 00:26:33.300
Everybody has to be on the team.

00:26:33.300 --> 00:26:36.230
So I, I every skill team I invited.

00:26:36.230 --> 00:26:40.880
So engineering, manufacturing, legal,
communications, every skill team, was now

00:26:40.880 --> 00:26:42.850
on the team, on the leadership team, all
reporting to me.

00:26:44.082 --> 00:26:48.890
And and all the business leaders from
around the world,

00:26:48.890 --> 00:26:52.380
Asia Pacific, Americas, all there, and
then we started, what

00:26:52.380 --> 00:26:55.030
we do, what I've always done with big
airplane program,

00:26:55.030 --> 00:26:57.700
is that I have a weekly meeting, where we
review.

00:26:57.700 --> 00:26:59.880
Everything associated with the plan,
everything.

00:26:59.880 --> 00:27:01.800
So we meet at seven o'clock in the
morning, because we're trying

00:27:01.800 --> 00:27:05.880
to honor, time changes in Shanghai, and,
and the Australia and everything else.

00:27:05.880 --> 00:27:07.900
So we've got the clocks all up on the
wall.

00:27:07.900 --> 00:27:10.370
We're all interneted, connected on the
internet.

00:27:10.370 --> 00:27:13.470
We have screens that were on the round
table, we are

00:27:13.470 --> 00:27:16.330
seeing all the leaders where ever they are
around the world.

00:27:16.330 --> 00:27:17.310
[SOUND] One set of charts.

00:27:17.310 --> 00:27:18.619
320 charts.

00:27:20.030 --> 00:27:22.530
All of the plan, whether it's income
statement, balance

00:27:22.530 --> 00:27:25.290
sheet, launches of new vehicles, it's all,
blue bars.

00:27:25.290 --> 00:27:27.630
There's a forecast, a red diamond, which
is,

00:27:27.630 --> 00:27:29.990
that, that leaves assessment for how it's
going.

00:27:29.990 --> 00:27:32.700
Then that, there's a, they risk and
opportunities, all

00:27:32.700 --> 00:27:36.030
the risk have been identified, the
opportunities have been monetized.

00:27:36.030 --> 00:27:39.210
And so, we're looking also five years out,
so when we complete the

00:27:39.210 --> 00:27:42.904
performance like the 6.6, or you could
also say an operating profit, 8.3.

00:27:42.904 --> 00:27:44.495
I just might toss that in.

00:27:44.495 --> 00:27:44.995
[LAUGH].

00:27:46.220 --> 00:27:49.060
&gt;&gt; that, everybody knows what the plan is,
everybody knows what the status

00:27:49.060 --> 00:27:51.940
of the plan is, and everybody knows the
areas that need special attention.

00:27:51.940 --> 00:27:54.905
When you do it together, the mean goes
from seven to.

00:27:54.905 --> 00:28:02.160
About 7 to 9.30, and then, we have guests
there, from around the world, from the

00:28:02.160 --> 00:28:05.690
engineering, manufacturing, all, all
watching, and we meet

00:28:05.690 --> 00:28:07.470
them, and we get their feedback at the
end.

00:28:07.470 --> 00:28:11.190
So you can imagine how, hoe transparent
and, and close you get.

00:28:11.190 --> 00:28:13.180
Now when we first started this.

00:28:13.180 --> 00:28:15.390
Remember I told you that, that within a
couple of

00:28:15.390 --> 00:28:18.920
days the forecast was that we were gonna
lose $17 billion.

00:28:18.920 --> 00:28:21.440
So I started the business plan review, the
charts are flowing,

00:28:21.440 --> 00:28:26.500
320 charts, we even have them color coded,
red, yellow, green.

00:28:26.500 --> 00:28:29.640
Any change in the chart is in blue, so
there's lots

00:28:29.640 --> 00:28:31.640
that doesn't change, all you're looking
for is what has changed.

00:28:31.640 --> 00:28:34.680
You don't want to hear a long explanation
about what, what's going on.

00:28:34.680 --> 00:28:36.320
But what you want is that, everybody knows

00:28:36.320 --> 00:28:38.800
the plan, everybody knows the areas of
special attention.

00:28:38.800 --> 00:28:41.810
So the color you got, you got the charts
going,

00:28:41.810 --> 00:28:44.700
and I, there's about three or four weeks
of data flowing.

00:28:44.700 --> 00:28:51.180
And all the charts are green, and I, I
stopped the meeting and I said guys.

00:28:52.540 --> 00:28:56.285
We're gonna be $17 billion, is there
anything that's not going well?

00:28:56.285 --> 00:29:00.310
[LAUGH].

00:29:00.310 --> 00:29:02.050
&gt;&gt; Eye contact, goes to the floor.

00:29:03.220 --> 00:29:04.920
Nobody says anything.

00:29:04.920 --> 00:29:08.200
Now remember that closure yes about, it
wasn't okay,

00:29:08.200 --> 00:29:11.390
to bring things up, I mean there's command
and control,.

00:29:11.390 --> 00:29:12.718
You know, people disappeared.

00:29:12.718 --> 00:29:13.596
[LAUGH].

00:29:13.596 --> 00:29:19.460
&gt;&gt; So, I think that, and then a week went
by and they're green.

00:29:19.460 --> 00:29:21.880
And, and of course they got me.

00:29:21.880 --> 00:29:23.100
They got this new leader.

00:29:23.100 --> 00:29:24.090
What, what's this leader gonna do?

00:29:24.090 --> 00:29:31.290
And, so the next two weeks later Mark
Fields.

00:29:31.290 --> 00:29:36.052
He was a, leader of all the Americas
business, Canada, the United States and

00:29:36.052 --> 00:29:38.093
South America had an edge avant, in

00:29:38.093 --> 00:29:40.815
Oakville, Canada and then actuator issue,
on

00:29:40.815 --> 00:29:43.743
the, tailgate, so he stopped production
because

00:29:43.743 --> 00:29:45.919
we're gonna be best in class, we're

00:29:45.919 --> 00:29:50.376
not gonna deliver one vehicle, unless it's
done and is the best in quality.

00:29:50.376 --> 00:29:52.431
So he had 2 or 3,000 edges.

00:29:52.431 --> 00:29:55.582
You know, sitting out on the tundra, think
I was cold, so it went sinking in.

00:29:55.582 --> 00:29:57.214
Cuz when you stop production.

00:29:57.214 --> 00:30:00.816
I mean, it's a big deal.

00:30:00.816 --> 00:30:03.140
And so up comes his chart.

00:30:03.140 --> 00:30:04.140
For the launch of this new edge.

00:30:04.140 --> 00:30:05.730
And it's bright red.

00:30:08.690 --> 00:30:10.660
And I mean, you, it got so quiet.

00:30:10.660 --> 00:30:14.545
I, I, you know what they're all thinking,
it's over, Mark's gone,

00:30:14.545 --> 00:30:17.691
[NOISE] he's out of here, and what's this
new guy gonna do?

00:30:17.691 --> 00:30:21.681
So, I started to clap now they knew that
was a sign the

00:30:21.681 --> 00:30:26.692
door was gonna open someone was gonna come
in Mark's out of here.

00:30:26.692 --> 00:30:30.745
So I could just, I could just feel it I
mean, it just and

00:30:30.745 --> 00:30:37.300
I said Mark is there anything that we can
do to help you with that?

00:30:37.300 --> 00:30:41.400
And before Mark could say one word, Benny

00:30:41.400 --> 00:30:44.210
Fowler who is the head of quality now
world

00:30:44.210 --> 00:30:46.820
wide, said Mark, I think I've seen that
issue

00:30:46.820 --> 00:30:49.010
on a launch that we did six months ago.

00:30:49.010 --> 00:30:51.420
Because you know in the car business you
have

00:30:51.420 --> 00:30:53.330
so much product coming out and that's
what's so exciting.

00:30:55.090 --> 00:30:57.250
And then Joe Hendricks, at the time, he's
a leader of [UNKNOWN] now.

00:30:57.250 --> 00:31:00.400
Was the header of a manufacturer, and he
said you

00:31:00.400 --> 00:31:02.710
gonna need some manufacturer engineers,
cuz as soon as you

00:31:02.710 --> 00:31:04.140
find the problem and fix it, you're gonna
have to

00:31:04.140 --> 00:31:06.560
change all these vehicles and get the
production going again.

00:31:06.560 --> 00:31:10.930
I'll have those, I'll have our dynamite
talent up in Canada immediately.

00:31:12.400 --> 00:31:16.000
And then Derek Cusack who leads product
development worldwide,

00:31:18.020 --> 00:31:20.600
says Mark I've seen that technical issue
on

00:31:20.600 --> 00:31:22.760
such and such five years ago or something.

00:31:22.760 --> 00:31:24.530
I'll get right on that.

00:31:24.530 --> 00:31:26.010
That exchange took 12 seconds.

00:31:28.300 --> 00:31:29.060
12 seconds.

00:31:30.660 --> 00:31:32.330
We're on to the next chart.

00:31:32.330 --> 00:31:34.603
Course it was green.

00:31:34.603 --> 00:31:36.170
[LAUGH] On the next shot, it's green.

00:31:37.880 --> 00:31:40.880
The next week I think it was still red.

00:31:40.880 --> 00:31:41.860
Mark's chart.

00:31:41.860 --> 00:31:43.600
Everything else is green.

00:31:43.600 --> 00:31:46.210
Next week I think he changed it to yellow

00:31:46.210 --> 00:31:50.040
because they found a solution and now
they're implementing it.

00:31:50.040 --> 00:31:55.180
I think the next week, it turned to green
and boom, all of

00:31:55.180 --> 00:32:00.390
the vehicles started going and then,
probably, one of the most exciting

00:32:00.390 --> 00:32:05.568
days of my life both from an oh, shit, I
mean this is a terrible situation.

00:32:05.568 --> 00:32:09.142
[LAUGH] Sorry, so sorry.

00:32:09.142 --> 00:32:10.210
[LAUGH].

00:32:10.210 --> 00:32:12.500
&gt;&gt; To my gosh, we're gonna make it.

00:32:13.790 --> 00:32:18.220
Was the following week, guess what the
charts looked like:?

00:32:18.220 --> 00:32:19.045
They looked like a rainbow.

00:32:19.045 --> 00:32:21.480
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Like a rainbow.

00:32:22.930 --> 00:32:27.390
And I'm, I'm going, oh, my goodness.

00:32:27.390 --> 00:32:29.200
I'm now the data says.

00:32:29.200 --> 00:32:31.370
Right here, why we're losing 17 billion
dollars.

00:32:33.400 --> 00:32:34.550
Cuz the data sets you free, right?

00:32:35.860 --> 00:32:36.880
Data tells you everything.

00:32:38.060 --> 00:32:43.270
But, also now, it was safe enough that you
could share how it was.

00:32:43.270 --> 00:32:45.660
You weren't red, the issue you're working
on is red.

00:32:45.660 --> 00:32:49.610
And, matter of fact, the expectation is
that

00:32:49.610 --> 00:32:52.390
everybody really does know what the
situation is.

00:32:52.390 --> 00:32:53.670
Cuz you can't manage a secret.

00:32:53.670 --> 00:32:56.840
People can't help if they don't know what
the real situation is.

00:32:56.840 --> 00:32:58.520
And it's safe and you're not gonna get a
[UNKNOWN].

00:32:58.520 --> 00:33:01.420
Now you can imagine the accountability
around the table.

00:33:01.420 --> 00:33:04.560
Are you gonna be read on a item and then
you're gonna go through the

00:33:04.560 --> 00:33:08.640
week and come back and say to all your
colleagues I was really busy last week.

00:33:08.640 --> 00:33:10.090
I didn't have a chance to work on that.

00:33:11.880 --> 00:33:15.300
And the pressure in a positive way is like
fantastic.

00:33:15.300 --> 00:33:18.620
Cuz everybody there is trying to figure
out how to help go forward.

00:33:18.620 --> 00:33:23.340
So in that one day it was probably, I was
at, it was probably like, oh my gosh.

00:33:23.340 --> 00:33:26.210
This is really in bad shape.

00:33:26.210 --> 00:33:27.200
But we all knew that.

00:33:27.200 --> 00:33:29.550
On the other hand, I knew at that moment
that

00:33:29.550 --> 00:33:30.740
we were going to be able to turn Ford
around.

00:33:32.740 --> 00:33:34.860
So that's my, can I, can I tell you one
more?

00:33:38.370 --> 00:33:39.810
okay, so here's another one.

00:33:39.810 --> 00:33:42.700
In this thing about vision and, and
everybody understanding.

00:33:42.700 --> 00:33:44.750
So I wanna tell you about the first time I
drove

00:33:44.750 --> 00:33:48.360
in the garage of the World Headquarters of
the Ford Motor Company.

00:33:48.360 --> 00:33:49.065
How we doing on time?

00:33:49.065 --> 00:33:51.270
[INAUDIBLE] 15 minutes, okay.

00:33:53.290 --> 00:33:55.970
So I left Boeing and I'm coming to Ford.

00:33:55.970 --> 00:33:56.470
Ford.

00:33:57.510 --> 00:33:58.520
Ford.

00:33:58.520 --> 00:34:02.460
I drive into the garage of the world
headquarters of the Ford Motor Company.

00:34:04.190 --> 00:34:08.180
And I drive in, there's not one Ford
vehicle in the garage.

00:34:10.000 --> 00:34:15.650
I know, I know, and I just left Boeing to
come to Ford and there

00:34:15.650 --> 00:34:20.980
all these Ashton Martens and Jaguars and,
and I, I remember thinking to myself I

00:34:20.980 --> 00:34:24.280
wonder what all the people in this
building are working on I don't think it's

00:34:24.280 --> 00:34:28.890
Ford and it was Ford was 85% of the
business but Ford was kind of.

00:34:31.160 --> 00:34:34.720
And, then I remember walking up and then
walking in that office like I shared

00:34:34.720 --> 00:34:38.520
with you and I knew, I knew it right away,
what we had to do.

00:34:38.520 --> 00:34:41.220
And you can imagine when the culture
change.

00:34:41.220 --> 00:34:44.120
Can you imagine being with all those
different brands, we had

00:34:44.120 --> 00:34:48.690
97 different models, that we were trying
